// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! Higher-level `Cache` tests: fetch (via a mock `Transport`, never the
//! network) + verify-before-cache + soft-fail, plus end-to-end
//! `discoverResponderUrl` against a real certificate.
//!
//! ## Fixture provenance
//!
//! `build.zig`'s module graph gives `ocspcache` only `ocsp` + `http` + `x509`
//! (not `rsa`/`p256` — those are `ocsp`'s own private deps, not transitive
//! across the module boundary), so this test file cannot generate RSA-signed
//! fixtures itself. The byte arrays below are **not captured from a public
//! CA**: they were generated by a throwaway offline generator
//! (`ocsp`'s own `der_writer` + `rsa.signPkcs1v15`/`rsa.selfSignedCert`, the
//! same construction `ocsp`'s own `ocsp_test.zig` does — see ocsp/SPEC.md
//! "Fixture provenance") invoked directly via `zig build-exe` with the same
//! module graph `build.zig` wires, entirely outside this repo's build
//! graph/CI and never committed. What's baked in:
//!
//! - `issuer_der_bytes` — an RSA CA cert (`rsa.selfSignedCert`, fixed seed).
//! - `subject_with_aia_bytes` / `subject_with_aia2_bytes` — leaf certs signed
//!   by the same issuer key, each hand-built (`rsa.selfSignedCert` has no
//!   extension hook for Authority Information Access) with an AIA extension
//!   whose `id-ad-ocsp` entry points at `responder_url`; distinct serials
//!   (0x77 / 0x79) so they hash to distinct cache keys.
//! - `subject_no_aia_bytes` — the same leaf shape, serial 0x78, no AIA
//!   extension at all.
//! - `good_response_bytes` / `good_response2_bytes` / `good_response3_bytes`
//!   — a `BasicOCSPResponse` (good status, `thisUpdate`/`nextUpdate` fixed at
//!   2027-01-01 / 2027-02-01) for each subject's own `CertID`, signed by the
//!   issuer key — a real signature over real DER, verifiable by `ocsp.verify`
//!   exactly as a fetched responder reply would be.
//! - `tampered_response_bytes` — `good_response_bytes` with one byte flipped
//!   inside the signature (structure intact, signature invalid).
//!
//! Regenerate: see the generator kept alongside this note in the task record
//! (fixed seed `0xfeed5eed`); nothing here is hand-edited binary.

